## Step 4: AlphaFold2 Structure Prediction

**Script:** `scripts/step4_alphafold2.py`  
**Tool:** ColabFold — https://colab.research.google.com/github/sokrypton/ColabFold/blob/main/AlphaFold2.ipynb

### Method

The full 928 aa pRb sequence was submitted to **ColabFold** using:
- MSA mode: `mmseqs2_uniref_env`
- Models: 5 predicted models ranked by pLDDT
- Pair mode: `unpaired_paired`
- Seed: default

### pLDDT Confidence Plot

![pLDDT per position](figures/plddt.png)

**Interpretation:**
- Structured domains (positions ~75–700): pLDDT **90–97** — very high confidence
- Disordered loop regions (sharp dips to 25–40): expected, these are flexible linkers between helices
- C-terminus (positions ~800–928): pLDDT 30–65 — partially disordered, consistent with known biology
- All 5 models agree closely — prediction is consistent and reliable

### Sequence Coverage

![Sequence coverage](figures/coverage.png)

**Interpretation:**
- 1,000–1,600 homologous sequences aligned per position — excellent MSA depth
- Orange/teal coloring indicates moderate-to-high identity homologs were found
- Coverage dips align exactly with pLDDT dips — confirming those regions are genuinely disordered

### Predicted Alignment Error (PAE)

![PAE heatmap](figures/pae.png)

**Interpretation:**
- **Blue diagonal blocks** (rank_1, rank_2): high confidence in intra-domain residue positions
- **Red off-diagonal regions**: uncertainty in relative domain positioning — expected because the disordered spacer acts as a flexible hinge between Pocket A and Pocket B
- rank_1 shows the most confident prediction — used as best model

### 3D Structure (RCSB Viewer)

![pRb 3D structure](figures/rcsb_structure.png)

The structure shows the dense helical core of the Pocket A and B domains (ribbons) and the disordered loop regions extending outward (thin lines) — exactly consistent with known pRb architecture.

### Summary

| Metric | Result |
|---|---|
| Tool | ColabFold (AlphaFold2) |
| Best model | rank_001 |
| Peak pLDDT | ~97 (structured domains) |
| MSA depth | 1,000–1,600 sequences |
| Model agreement | All 5 ranks consistent |
| Validation | Intra-domain PAE confirms folded Pocket A/B |

**Output files:** `outputs/AlphaFold2_report.txt`, `figures/plddt.png`, `figures/pae.png`, `figures/coverage.png`

---

## Step 5: GNINA Molecular Docking

**Script:** `scripts/step5_gnina_docking.py`  
**Tool:** GNINA v1.1 — https://github.com/gnina/gnina

### Ligand: Palbociclib (Ibrance)

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| Drug name | Palbociclib (Ibrance) |
| PubChem CID | 5330286 |
| Class | CDK4/6 inhibitor |
| MW | 447.54 Da |
| Clinical use | HR+/HER2− advanced breast cancer |
| Rationale | Prevents CDK4/6 from phosphorylating pRb → keeps pRb active → re-activates RB1 checkpoint |

### GNINA Command

```bash
./gnina \
    -r receptor.pdb \
    -l palbociclib.sdf \
    --autobox_ligand receptor.pdb \
    --exhaustiveness 8 \
    --num_modes 9 \
    --cnn_scoring rescore \
    -o docking_output.sdf \
    --log docking_log.txt \
    --seed 42
```

### Docking Results (All 9 Poses)

| Mode | Affinity (kcal/mol) | Intramol (kcal/mol) | CNN Pose Score | CNN Affinity |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **1 ★** | -5.83 | 0.35 | **0.3842** | 5.556 |
| 2 | -5.99 | -0.45 | 0.3453 | 6.036 |
| 3 | -5.34 | 0.30 | 0.3291 | 5.711 |
| 4 | -5.44 | -0.40 | 0.2572 | 5.360 |
| 5 | -7.17 | 1.10 | 0.1971 | 5.369 |
| 6 | -6.34 | 1.08 | 0.1869 | 4.878 |
| 7 | -5.87 | -0.59 | 0.1819 | 4.885 |
| 8 | -5.59 | 0.29 | 0.1781 | 5.400 |
| 9 | -5.86 | -0.43 | 0.1738 | 5.144 |

★ **Best pose = Mode 1** (highest CNN pose score: 0.3842, affinity: −5.83 kcal/mol)

### Docking Visualization (Molstar)

![GNINA docking result](figures/docking_molstar.png)

The **blue/teal molecule (Palbociclib)** is visible docked inside the helical core of pRb (orange). It sits within the central pocket region, consistent with engagement of the binding groove.

### Interpretation

- **CNN Pose Score 0.3842**: GNINA's neural network ranks this as the most geometrically plausible pose
- **Binding Affinity −5.83 to −7.17 kcal/mol**: moderate binding range, consistent with an exploratory docking study
- **Mode 1 vs Mode 5**: Mode 5 has a stronger Vina score (−7.17) but much lower CNN confidence (0.1971) — Mode 1 is preferred as it balances energy and pose quality
- **Conclusion**: Palbociclib shows plausible direct engagement with the pRb pocket; its primary pharmacological mechanism remains CDK4/6 inhibition upstream of pRb

**Output files:** `outputs/docking_log.txt`, `outputs/docking_output.sdf`

